      <section class="prose" aria-labelledby="gist">
        <p class="eyebrow">The gist</p>
        <h2 id="gist">Four questions, no defaults</h2>
        <p>
          Most applications today are limited less by CPU than by data: how much there is,
          how complex it is, and how fast it changes. Those applications are built from the
          same few building blocks: databases, caches, search indexes, stream processors and
          batch jobs. Chapter 1 doesn't explain how any of them work. It explains the decisions
          that come <em>before</em> choosing them, and it frames each one as a spectrum rather
          than a right answer.
        </p>
      </section>

